\f0\fs24 \cf2 The Library still has all its charm, but if you look closely\'85 something has changed. The benches along the walls? Replaced with new cabinetry, perfectly in tune with the original ones. And the curtains that once concealed the books? Gone too! Now, you can finally admire the collection in all its splendor: over 2,500 volumes dedicated to art, architecture, and interior design. A treasure trove for anyone who loves discovering the world through its pages.\
The large table in the center, however, has stayed true to itself, enhanced by scientific objects that tell the story of the Bagatti Valsecchi brothers' passion for collecting.\
But there's a detail for true interior sleuths: the entrance you just passed through\'85 didn\'92t exist. Or rather, it was a secret door! Hidden, invisible, camouflaged. And it\'92s not the only one: there are three of them in this room. Can you find them all?}